# Root build context is only used by the backend service images (services/*/Dockerfile).
# Everything is left out except what their Maven build reads. A Jenkins workspace also holds the
# Maven repository (.m2) and the npm cache (.npm), which would otherwise be sent to Docker with
# every image build.
*
!pom.xml
!libs
!services
**/target
# The images are built with -DskipTests and hold no test code, so a change that only touches
# tests leaves every image's Maven build layer in the cache.
**/src/test
